WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.290
Winter 2013 to 2014.

2
00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:07.330
The Met Office called it the wettest
winter in England and Wales since at least

3
00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:09.610
1766.

4
00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:14.550
Across the UK, rain reached
165 per cent of average.

5
00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:19.330
In south-west England, most of the Somerset
Levels and Moors lie only a few metres

6
00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:21.010
above mean sea level.

7
00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:25.810
From mid-December 2013, farmland
and roads went under water.

8
00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:29.670
A whole winter's rain on
land barely above the sea.

9
00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:32.150
Why did the water stay for months?

10
00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:34.530
In this mission, you'll
build the chain of causes,

11
00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:37.130
from storm to standing water.

12
00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:39.690
Then you'll sort the
flood's effects on people,

13
00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:41.450
property and land.

14
00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:46.600
Your mission: explain why the floodwater
on the Somerset Levels stayed for months.
